This '''city''' was a major [[city]] on [[Concordia]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. [[Governor]] [[Pre Vizsla]] maintained a residence at the government complex there.<ref name="TMP" /> In [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' episode "[[Landing at Point Rain]]" to [[21 BBY]], and {{HelmetCollectionCite|76|Highlights of the Saga}} dates the [[death]] of [[Ponds]], as seen in the episode "[[Lethal Trackdown]]," to the same [[Standard year|year]]. Since {{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-chronological-episodeorder|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Chronological Episode Order}} places "[[The Mandalore Plot]]" between "Landing at Point Rain" and "Lethal Trackdown", its events must also take place in 21 [[Galactic Standard Calendar|BBY]].</ref> [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]] visited with the body of the [[Death Watch]] [[Death Watch bomber|bomber]] who [[Attack on the Memorial Shrine|destroyed]] the [[Peace Park]].<ref name="TMP" />

{{City-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
This unnamed city first appeared in ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the twelfth episode of the [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' television series']] [[The Clone Wars: Season Two|second season]], entitled "[[The Mandalore Plot]]."<ref name="TMP" />

